{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 46.6% a year from $6.91 billion in FY2017 to $215.9 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F211]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was not smooth: revenue fell 6.8% in FY2020 and was flat at 0.2% growth in FY2023 before jumping 125.9% in FY2024 and 114.2% in FY2025 [D130][D284][D338][D393]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2024 step change came from Data Center revenue up 217%, driven by Hopper GPU shipments for LLM training and inference [P22][P23]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 growth of 65.5% was again data center compute and networking, with Blackwell the majority of Data Center revenue [D448][P10]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Data Center was 89.7% of FY2026 revenue and contributed 60.2pp of the 65.5% growth [D620][D622][D448]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Within it, Data Center computing grew 59% on Blackwell demand and networking grew 142% on NVLink for GB200 and GB300 systems [P8]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Compute was 75.2% of revenue and added 46.1pp, while Networking added 14.1pp on 141.5% growth [D627][D629][D636]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 60.1% against revenue growth of 65.5%, so incremental operating margin was 57.3% [D449][D448][D475]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS rose 66.7% against net income growth of 64.7%, with the diluted share count down 1.2% [D452][D450][D470]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin was 60.4% in FY2026, against a window median of 32.8%, a high of 62.4% in FY2025 and a low of 15.7% in FY2023 [F50][D813][D812][D811]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin fell 3.9pp to 71.1%, the main drag on the 2.0pp operating-margin decline [F30][D462][D463]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Compute & Networking operating income absorbed a $4.5 billion H20 excess inventory and purchase-obligation charge in the first quarter of FY2026 [P7]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "R&D rose 43.2% on a 29% increase in compensation and a 79% increase in compute and infrastructure, though it still added 1.3pp to margin [D466][P5][D478]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Net margin trailed operating margin by 4.8pp as other income of $11.1 billion, largely unrealized equity gains including Intel, lifted pre-tax income [D861][X120][P3]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $102.7 billion was 0.86x net income, the window low against a median of 0.97x [F100][F60][D435][D851]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow of $96.7 billion was a 44.8% margin, just under the 46.6% FY2025 high [F110][D432][D821]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex of $6.04 billion was 2.8% of revenue and 2.13x D&A, up from 1.74x in FY2025 [F105][D431][D437][D382]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Inventory grew 112.3% and receivables 66.8%, pushing days inventory to 125 and days sales outstanding to 65 [D474][D473][D446][D445]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Total debt was $8.47 billion against $10.6 billion of cash, and short-term investments were not reported in FY2026, so net cash is understated [D440][F150][R3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity was 101.5%, in the 100th percentile of six semis peers against a 20.3% median [D447][D848][D849]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $40.1 billion plus dividends of $974 million were 42.5% of free cash flow [X150][X160][D444]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Acquisitions of $1.54 billion and higher equity purchases drove investing outflow of $52.2 billion [X168][F120][P1]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Short-term investments were not reported in FY2026 after $34.6 billion in FY2025, so net cash and its peer rank omit them [R3][X188]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Two direct customers were 22% and 14% of FY2026 revenue, both mainly in Compute & Networking [P6]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "China revenue fell 21.4% in FY2026 and its share dropped to 9.1% from 19.2% [D545][D544][D541]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The Graphics segment was 44.1% of revenue and fell 25.0% in FY2023, a past cyclicality marker [D753][D754][R1]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "If gross margin falls below the FY2026 level of 71.1%, the H20 charge would look structural rather than one-off [F30]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "If operating cash flow to net income stays below the 0.86x FY2026 level, working-capital build is outpacing earnings [D435]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "If Data Center share drops below 89.7%, the concentration that drove the window would be diluting [D620]."}
  ]}
]}
